  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Readers can wait in several spots, and a quiet-waiting notice can be moved around the pickup area.\", \"decision\": \"How should the library encourage quieter waiting?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nStaff place the notice at the entrance with a simple map of quieter waiting spots. Readers can choose a suitable place before reaching the crowded desk.\nStaff place the quiet-waiting notice beside the waiting spots before the service starts. Readers encounter the expectation as they choose where to wait.\nA helper points out quieter waiting spots and then places the notice where readers have gathered. The reminder follows the actual waiting pattern."
    }
